# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# caches
.turbo/
.cache/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.tgz

# Windows shell cruft (this repo is developed on Windows)
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS resource forks, for anyone cloning on a Mac
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# editors / IDEs
# Keep shared workspace config committable, ignore everything personal.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# agent tooling — none of this belongs in a shared repo
#
# .claude/ holds per-developer AI-assistant config, not project config. Its
# settings.json is a permissions allowlist: it grants no new capability (anyone
# can already run `npm run build` in a terminal), it only suppresses confirmation
# prompts inside one tool. Committing it would decide on every teammate's behalf
# what their agent may run unprompted — that is a personal-machine setting, so it
# stays on personal machines. It also accumulates absolute paths like
# C:/Users/<name>/... and one-off session ids, which are pure noise to everyone else.
#
# .claude/skills/ is ~0.5 MB of Prisma vendor docs from `npx prisma init`. Also
# regenerable, and its skills were ABSOLUTE symlinks into .agents/skills — with
# core.symlinks=false (the Windows default) git commits those as text files
# containing "/c/Nikhil@pbn/pbn-proposal/...", which resolves to nothing on another
# machine, in CI, or after moving this folder.
#
# .agents/ and .windsurf/ have been deleted from this repo; the rules stay so a
# future `prisma init` doesn't quietly stage them again.
#
# NOTE: AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are deliberately NOT ignored. They document a real
# project constraint (this Next.js version differs from model training data), are
# read by several tools rather than one, and grant no permissions.
/.claude/
/.agents/
/.windsurf/
/skills-lock.json

# debug / logs
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# prisma
# The client is generated from prisma/schema.prisma on postinstall, so it is
# build output rather than source.
/src/generated/prisma/
#
# Do NOT ignore prisma/migrations/ — migration history is source of truth for
# the database and has to be committed and deployed.
